# clang-format is for C/C++ only; QML must never go through it.
# Patterns anchor to this file's directory and are matched fnmatch-style
# against the formatted file's absolute path; * and ? never cross "/", and
# only a "**/" segment does (matching zero or more directories), so
# "**/*.qml" ignores QML at any depth including this root, while a bare
# "*.qml" would only ignore files sitting directly in this root
# (semantics of clang-format 22 matchFilePath; keep the "**/").
# deno task format rejects non-C/C++ files before invoking clang-format;
# this stopgap covers raw clang-format runs. Ignored files are skipped
# silently (exit 0); clang-format --list-ignored <files> enumerates them.
*.qml
**/*.qml
